public class BadCommandExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String userInput = "rm -rf /"; // Malicious input
        String command = "ls " + userInput; // Vulnerable: User input in command
        Process process = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);
    }
}
```
**Fix:**
```java
// Good: Sanitize or use secure alternatives
public class SecureCommandExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String userInput = "rm -rf /"; // Still tested for robustness
        // Option 1: Sanitize input (e.g., allow only safe commands)
        if (!userInput.startsWith("ls ")) {
            throw new SecurityException("Command not allowed");
        }
        // Option 2: Use a sandboxed environment (e.g., Apache Guacamole)
        Process process = Runtime.getRuntime().exec("ls");
    }
}
